@startuml reaction-sequence
' One reader reacts to an article while a second reader has it open (api/reactions.ts, hooks/useReactions.ts).
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Times New Roman
actor "Reader A" as A
participant "Reactions /\nuseReactions (A)" as UA
participant "api/reactions" as API
participant "Appwrite TablesDB" as DB
participant "Appwrite Realtime" as RT
participant "useReactions (B)" as UB
A -> UA : open /blog/:slug
UA -> API : import() (separate chunk)
API -> RT : subscribe("row created", reactions)
note right of API : subscribe first, so a reaction made\nwhile counting is not missed (defect I12)
API -> DB : listRows(article, kind, limit 1) per kind
DB --> API : totals
UA --> A : buttons enabled, counts shown
A -> UA : click "Useful"
UA -> UA : mark pressed, remember in localStorage
UA -> API : addReaction(article, kind, visitor)
API -> DB : createRow(id = visitor-digest-kind)
alt row is new
  DB --> API : 201 created
  UA --> A : count + 1
  DB -> RT : row created
  RT -> UA : event for a row this tab wrote: ignored
  RT -> UB : event
  UB -> UB : count + 1
else row already exists (same reaction sent from another tab)
  DB --> API : 409 conflict, addReaction returns false
  UA --> A : count unchanged
end
@enduml
